<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Council of Fascism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fascist Grand Council</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascism">Fascism</a> was the supreme body of the Fascist regime in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. In July 1943, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allied-invasion-of-sicily">Allied invasion of Sicily</a>, it voted against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>, leading to his removal from power and marking the collapse of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a> and the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-council-of-fascism.jpg" alt="Grand Council of Fascism" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lesser_coat_of_arms_of_the_Kingdom_of_Italy_(1929-1943).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
